Bug fix: lobby Co-op/PvP/PvPvE panel no longer overlays mode buttons.

This commit modifies 1 file (+32/-1 lines), touching 1 task/ops files file.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
Root cause: lobbyOptionsPanel (Co-op/PvP/PvPvE + win conditions) was
position:fixed at top:50% -200px, overlapping modeSelectorDiv (Waves/
King/etc.) at top:38%. The two fixed panels occupied the same screen area.

Fix in src/network-main.ts:
- Removed position:fixed, top/left/transform/z-index from lobbyOptionsPanel
- Changed document.body.appendChild to modeSelectorDiv.appendChild
- Added margin-top:14px for visual separation

Panel now flows naturally below game mode buttons instead of overlaying.
